#{[:db/ident :activity.type/assignment {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045461 :db/ident :activity.type/assignment}] [:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank}] [:db/ident :answer-field.type/free {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408167 :db/ident :answer-field.type/free}] [:db/ident :answer.type/math {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math}] [:db/ident :answer.type/text {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text}] [:db/ident :course-academy.source/editor {:db/doc "User-directed content formatting edits in Course Academy." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502323 :db/ident :course-academy.source/editor}] [:course/id #uuid "c37c596e-77c4-5554-8295-443fb5da076b" {:course/code "MTH 255" :course/description "Vector Calculus II develops the calculus of vector fields and integration along curves and over surfaces. Building on Vector Calculus I, the course connects local descriptions of a field with accumulated quantities such as work, circulation, and flux. Its central tools include conservative fields, divergence, curl, and the integral theorems of Gauss and Stokes, with applications involving force, work, mass, and charge." :course/id #uuid "c37c596e-77c4-5554-8295-443fb5da076b" :course/outcomes [{:course-outcome/category "Differential Operators and Integral Theorems" :course-outcome/id #uuid "8b26130c-3ade-59f1-b5cd-30c4e77a4ee2" :course-outcome/index 9 :course-outcome/text "Explain and apply the Divergence Theorem to connect flux through a closed surface with a volume integral." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406505} {:course-outcome/category "Differential Operators and Integral Theorems" :course-outcome/id #uuid "11744f40-4941-5b05-bf74-21cff6dfbc86" :course-outcome/index 10 :course-outcome/text "Explain and apply Stokes’ Theorem to connect circulation around a boundary curve with a surface integral of curl." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406506} {:course-outcome/category "Differential Operators and Integral Theorems" :course-outcome/id #uuid "68ca80d7-e11e-58c2-9696-309503e57498" :course-outcome/index 8 :course-outcome/text "Calculate divergence and curl in standard coordinate systems and interpret them in relation to flux and circulation." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406507} {:course-outcome/category "Line Integrals and Conservative Fields" :course-outcome/id #uuid "9cd133e0-c54b-57f1-b597-4c2164a5bb07" :course-outcome/index 5 :course-outcome/text "Analyze conservative fields, find potential functions when they exist, and use path independence to evaluate line integrals." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406508} {:course-outcome/category "Line Integrals and Conservative Fields" :course-outcome/id #uuid "da10e544-4158-5cc3-9189-961bf8e19bf4" :course-outcome/index 4 :course-outcome/text "Evaluate scalar and vector line integrals and interpret their use in calculating quantities such as mass, work, and circulation." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406509} {:course-outcome/category "Surface Integrals and Flux" :course-outcome/id #uuid "c94983bd-7208-5af7-ab33-1ac7d94075a5" :course-outcome/index 6 :course-outcome/text "Set up and evaluate scalar surface integrals for quantities distributed over a surface, including mass or charge." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406510} {:course-outcome/category "Surface Integrals and Flux" :course-outcome/id #uuid "25423c4b-02b3-5fec-9546-7129ca1e1f95" :course-outcome/index 7 :course-outcome/text "Calculate flux through an oriented surface and interpret the role of the field’s normal component." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406511} {:course-outcome/category "Vector Geometry and Field Interpretation" :course-outcome/id #uuid "b93f8b7e-2e08-5fbc-b3b3-5fd74c01da7c" :course-outcome/index 2 :course-outcome/text "Explain the relationship among gradients, directional derivatives, and level sets." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406512} {:course-outcome/category "Vector Geometry and Field Interpretation" :course-outcome/id #uuid "3561ac1e-b8dd-59c8-b44a-28a8ad8f9fdc" :course-outcome/index 1 :course-outcome/text "Express vectors in standard coordinate systems and bases and interpret dot and cross products geometrically." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406513} {:course-outcome/category "Vector Geometry and Field Interpretation" :course-outcome/id #uuid "6ad6c8c5-38f2-5456-9c16-b54686cf0083" :course-outcome/index 3 :course-outcome/text "Construct line and surface elements appropriate to a curve or surface, accounting for its geometry and orientation." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406514}] :course/overview "The course revisits vector functions, space curves, gradients, and directional derivatives before extending integration to curves and surfaces. Line integrals connect vector fields with work and circulation. Conservative fields, potential functions, and path independence explain when an integral can be determined from endpoint information rather than the details of a path.\n\nSurface geometry and oriented surface elements provide the foundation for surface integrals and flux. Divergence and curl describe local field behavior, while the Divergence Theorem and Stokes’ Theorem connect these local quantities to integrals over regions and their boundaries. The archived course materials emphasize geometric understanding and the use of vector differentials to connect the various integration methods." :course/school "Oregon State University" :course/title "Vector Calculus II" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405204}] [:topic/math-academy-id 283 {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050057 :topic/difficulty 1.2923920556013409 :topic/id #uuid "29efff6a-8254-59b2-b3ad-421a4dead37e" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064196} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064197} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064198}] :topic/math-academy-id 283 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050571}] :topic/title "The Fundamental Theorem of Calculus"}] [:topic/math-academy-id 997 {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050860 :topic/difficulty 0.9339225415057509 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429734 :encompassing/ratio